SLICE 0 HARNESS — runnable from the lane-b worktree, and one broken-instrument finding.
2026-08-04T01:32:11Z

== WHY THIS WAS NEEDED ==
web/public/bible/ (198 MB, 18 translations) and data/ are gitignored and exist only in the
main clone, so both frozen scripts died at readdirSync from this worktree. The freeze rule
forbids editing them to fix it. Resolved WITHOUT touching them: web/public/bible is a symlink
to the main clone (gitignored, invisible to git); the input volume is passed as an absolute
path, because both scripts already take it as process.argv[2] -- so data/ needs no symlink,
which matters because data/ is NOT gitignored and a symlink there would be committable.

